1
00:02:27,087 --> 00:02:29,566
<v WOMAN> Good evening.King's Restaurant.


2
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:34,528
<v MAN>Good evening.I'm ringing about the job I understand you have vacant.


3
00:02:34,528 --> 00:02:35,295
<v WOMAN> Oh yes

4
00:02:35,295 --> 00:02:38,006
<v MAN> I'd like to find out a few more details,if i may.

5
00:02:38,006 --> 00:02:38,106
<v WOMAN>Yes,of course.Can i take your name?

6
00:02:40,146 --> 00:02:42,027
<v MAN> It's Peter Chin.


7
00:02:42,027 --> 00:02:50,556
<v WOMAN> Okay Peter.Well,if you want to ask about the job and then if we're both still interested, we could arrange for you to come for an interview.


8
00:02:50,556 --> 00:02:57,072
<v MAN> Great,thanks.I'm afraid i missed the advert for the job but heard about it from a friend.


9
00:02:57,072 --> 00:03:00,145
<v WOMAN>That's no problem at all.What would you like to know?


10
00:03:00,145 --> 00:03:04,335
<v MAN> Well,um,what sort of work is it - washing up?


11
00:03:04,335 --> 00:03:06,312
<v WOMAN> It's answering the phone.


12
00:03:06,312 --> 00:03:08,667
<v MAN> Oh right,fine.


13
00:03:08,667 --> 00:03:11,299
<v WOMAN>And not waiting at table.


14
00:03:11,299 --> 00:03:15,707
<v MAN> That'd be good.And how many nights a week would it be?


15
00:03:15,707 --> 00:03:18,564
<v WOMAN> Well,we're really only busy at the weekend.


16
00:03:18,564 --> 00:03:20,518
<v MAN> So two nights?


17
00:03:20,518 --> 00:03:24,598
<v WOMAN>Three actually,so it would work out at twelve hours a week.


18
00:03:24,598 --> 00:03:27,720
<v MAN>That'd be fine.It wouldn't interfere with my studies.


19
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,242
<v WOMAN> Are you at the university?

20
00:03:29,232 --> 00:03:31,317
<v MAN>Yes.First year Physics student.
 

21
00:03:31,317 --> 00:03:32,255
<v WOMAN> On.right.

22
00:03:32,255 --> 00:03:38,033
<v MAN>Um,and because i'm not an EU national would i need a work permit?


23
00:03:38,033 --> 00:03:40,965
<v WOMAN> Yes you would. Just get your tutor to sign it.


24
00:03:40,965 --> 00:03:47,390
<v MAN> That wouldn't be a problem,if i were to get the job.Um,where exactly is the restaurant?


25
00:03:47,390 --> 00:03:53,104
<v WOMAN> Well,we have two branches - the one we're recruiting for is in Hillsdunne Road.


26
00:03:53,104 --> 00:03:57,360
<v MAN>I don't know that.How do you spell it please?


27
00:03:57,350 --> 00:04:03,831
<v WOMAN> It's H-I-double L-S-D-U-double N-E Road.


28
00:04:03,821 --> 00:04:08,592
<v MAN>Got that.Thanks.is it near a bus stop?
 

29
00:04:08,592 --> 00:04:12,297
<v WOMAN>Yes. The nearest one would probably be just beside the Library.


30
00:04:12,297 --> 00:04:18,549
<v MAN>Oh yes,i know it.That'd be fine for me.And could i ask about the pay?


31
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:21,567
<v WOMAN>We're offering￡4.45 an hour.


32
00:04:21,567 --> 00:04:25,666
<v MAN> That's very good.My last job was ￡3.95 an hour.


33
00:04:25,666 --> 00:05:17,993
<v WOMAN>We feel it's pretty good and we also offer some good fringe benefits.


34
00:05:17,983 --> 00:05:18,726
<v MAN>Really?


35
00:05:18,726 --> 00:05:21,723
<v WOMAN> Well,we give you a free dinner,so you eat well.


36
00:05:21,723 --> 00:05:24,259
<v MAN> Right,better than hostel food!


37
00:05:24,259 --> 00:05:29,729
<v WOMAN>We certainly hope so! And we also offer extra pay for working on national holidays.


38
00:05:29,729 --> 00:05:31,855
<v MAN> Oh,that's a really good perk,isn't it?


39
00:05:31,855 --> 00:05:39,399
<v WOMAN> Yes,we think so.And then because of the difficulties of getting public transport, if you're working after 11 o'clock we drive you home.


40
00:05:39,399 --> 00:05:41,068
<v MAN>Oh,that's good to know.


41
00:05:41,068 --> 00:05:46,536
<v WOMAN>well,we'd certainly be interested in inviting you for an interview,if you're still interested?


42
00:05:46,536 --> 00:05:52,678
<v MAN> Oh yes,certainly.Could I just also ask what qualities you're looking for?

43
00:05:52,678 --> 00:05:59,278
<v WOMAN>Well,for this particular job we want a clear voice,which you obviously do have!


44
00:05:59,278 --> 00:06:01,351
<v MAN>Thank.


45
00:06:01,351 --> 00:06:04,330
<v WOMAN> And you must be able to think quickly,you know.


46
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:06,050
<v MAN> Well,i hope i'd...


47
00:06:06,050 --> 00:06:10,996
<v WOMAN> So,when could you come in for an interview?We're actually quite quiet tonight?


48
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:19,377
<v MAN>Sorry,I couldn't come tonight.Or tomorrow,I'm afraid.Thursday's okay that'd be 22nd of October.


49
00:06:19,377 --> 00:06:21,263
<v WOMAN>Fine,after 5 p.m.?


50
00:06:21,263 --> 00:06:24,471
<v MAN> Yes,fine.Would 6 o'clock be okay?


51
00:06:24,471 --> 00:06:28,578
<v WOMAN> Perfect.And could you bring along the names of two referees?


52
00:06:28,578 --> 00:06:30,541
<v MAN> Yes,that's fine,no problem.

53
00:06:30,541 --> 00:06:32,868
<v WOMAN> Good,I look forward to seeing you.

54
00:06:32,868 --> 00:06:36,249
<v MAN>Oh,by the way,who should i ask for?


55
00:06:36,249 --> 00:06:40,033
<v WOMAN>Oh yes ,of course,sorry.My name is Samira Manuja.

56
00:06:40,033 --> 00:06:42,397
<v MAN>Can you spell that,please?


57
00:06:42,397 --> 00:06:46,297
<v WOMAN> M-A-N-U-J-A.


58
00:06:46,297 --> 00:06:50,619
<v MAN> Okay.i've got that.Thanks very much.


59
00:06:50,619 --> 00:06:52,094
<v WOMAN>Look forward to seeing you...